@startuml
allowmixing
title Boussinesq solver - package context

package "process" {
  class Flow
}

package "hydromodpy.solver.boussinesq" {
  class Boussinesq
  class BoussinesqMesh
  class BoussinesqState
  class "solver_contract.py" as SolverContractModule <<module>>
  class "runtime_selection.py" as RuntimeSelection <<module>>
  class "runtime_contract.py" as RuntimeContract <<module>>
  package methods
  package engines
  package formulations
  package discretization
  package "assembly/" as Assembly
  package "drivers/" as Drivers
  package "forcing/" as Forcing
  package "jacobian/" as Jacobian
  package "runtimes/" as Runtimes
}

Flow --> Boussinesq : hydrological definition
Boussinesq --> BoussinesqMesh : builds and uses
Boussinesq --> SolverContractModule : normalizes regime, closure, options
Boussinesq --> RuntimeSelection : resolves method + engine
RuntimeSelection --> methods
RuntimeSelection --> engines
methods --> formulations
methods --> discretization
Boussinesq --> RuntimeContract : packages solve inputs
Boussinesq --> Drivers : steady and transient solves
Boussinesq --> Forcing : process to arrays
Drivers --> Runtimes : calls the selected runtime
Runtimes ..> Assembly : residual and fluxes
Runtimes ..> Jacobian : linearization
Boussinesq --> BoussinesqState : stores accepted state

note right of Boussinesq
Top-level orchestrator.
It delegates the solves, the forcing
translation and the summary shaping.
end note

note bottom of Assembly
Physical core.
One canonical boundary language:
prescribed boundary cells.
end note

@enduml
